# CLI and visualization

`cli` and `visualization` may import `bt.*` and `research.*`. They are not the math core.

For Streamlit UI, layouts, widgets, or theming, follow `.agents/skills/developing-with-streamlit/SKILL.md`. Verify in the running app, not by screenshot alone.

Residual fibre / layer / `N1` / `N0` / `Q` commands and the Residual explorer import `research.residuals`, not deleted `bt.calculus` paths.

```python
# BAD
from bt.calculus.cubic_fibres import fibre_of

# GOOD
from research.residuals.cubic_fibres import fibre_of
from research.residuals.stratum import newton_stratum
from bt.calculus.cubic import F_k
```

`btlab ui` launches the Streamlit app. Keep `btlab collatz ui` and `btlab calculus explorer`.
